Dragon Burst (2026-10-28): the velocity pass skipped when both the motion blur and the depth of field are off.

The per-pixel velocity pass (ucode 29D1F5CC913EBB07, the Renut's FE8B85F12835546D) feeds only the motion blur and
the depth of field composite; with both off nothing reads it. Mali-G57, 720p fight: GPU 25.3 -> 24.7 ms.

diff --git a/src/burstlimit_patches.cpp b/src/burstlimit_patches.cpp
--- a/src/burstlimit_patches.cpp
+++ b/src/burstlimit_patches.cpp
@@ -127,6 +127,10 @@
 // blurs over several pixels at higher resolutions. Skipped, the frame stays
 // as it was.
 constexpr uint64_t kSoftFilterShader = 0x04FCB369A8343665;
+// Dragon Burst: the per-pixel velocity pass (velocity from the linear depth and the camera's motion, written for the
+// motion blur; its z the depth the depth of field composite may read). Read only by those two: with both off it is
+// skipped (~0.6 ms of GPU at 720p on a Mali-G57, the same picture).
+constexpr uint64_t kVelocityShader = 0x29D1F5CC913EBB07;
 
 void ApplyPostEffectSettings() {
   std::vector<rex::graphics::PixelShaderDrawOverride> overrides;
@@ -148,6 +152,9 @@
